./evidence/ingests/react-hospitalrun/admission.json:188:      "finding": "Examined directly in the reconciled source. src/shared/config/pouchdb.ts registers pouchdb-authentication as a PouchDB plugin, but it only constructs a server database when process.env.NODE_ENV === 'test' (an in-memory adapter). In every non-test build `serverDb` is left undefined and the module still exports `export const remoteDb = serverDb as PouchDB.Database`. The four call sites — App.tsx `remoteDb.getSession()` on mount and user-slice.ts `logIn`, `getUser`, `logOut` — therefore dereference `undefined` at runtime rather than contacting a remote. App.tsx wraps the mount-time call in try/catch and only `console.log`s the failure before rendering, and no /login route is declared in the router at all.",
